{
  "description": "Tool labels for the investigation agent (utils/investigation.py), written before any agent output existed. For each case: the tools a careful analyst would need (required) and the tools that only check or restate what the record already says (acceptable). Any other tool called counts as unnecessary. Covers the development, held-out and no-rule sets and the ledger-backed set.",
  "tools": [
    "screen_party",
    "country_risk",
    "explain_rule",
    "party_history",
    "search_guidance"
  ],
  "policy": [
    "required: the decision depends on information the record does not state, and the tool returns it.",
    "acceptable: the tool only checks or restates what the record states, or gives context a careful analyst may reasonably consult.",
    "search_guidance: required when the expected verdict is SUSPICIOUS or the record carries a rule reason (the rationale must cite the regulatory basis, or why the rule does not make the payment suspicious); acceptable otherwise.",
    "screen_party: required where a party name carries a public-office title or names a coin-mixing service and no sanctions reason fired (N-05, N-06, N-12); acceptable everywhere else, since screening both parties is routine.",
    "country_risk: acceptable on every case, required on none. The record already states list membership, and the tool knows only the configured lists.",
    "explain_rule: acceptable where the record carries a rule reason or note; unnecessary otherwise.",
    "party_history: the development, held-out and no-rule cases have no ledger, so it is never required there; acceptable where the suspicion or the ambiguity concerns how an account behaves (structuring, layering, pass-through and over-threshold categories, PI-01, PI-02, N-01, N-07, N-08, N-09, N-11, N-13, N-14, N-15, N-17, N-18), unnecessary elsewhere. Ledger-backed cases: required on every case, on the beneficiary for fan-in and on the originator otherwise (required_role; reported separately, not part of tool precision or recall)."
  ],
